From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000011 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TB371FC Linux Project <tb371fc-linux@localhost>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 20:18:00 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: tb371fc: reject unpopulated DSC state

MSM mode_set populates the dynamic DSC fields before panel prepare.  Refuse
to start the TB371FC command table if that lifecycle contract is ever broken,
instead of transmitting a syntactically valid but unusable zero-filled PPS.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-novatek-nt36523.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-novatek-nt36523.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-novatek-nt36523.c
index a1443a9b0fa7..39843107bc0a 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-novatek-nt36523.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-novatek-nt36523.c
@@ -489,6 +489,15 @@ static int tb371fc_nt36532_init_sequence(struct panel_info *pinfo, bool boe)
 	struct mipi_dsi_multi_context dsi_ctx = { .dsi = NULL };
 	struct drm_dsc_picture_parameter_set pps;
 
+	if (!pinfo->dsc.slice_chunk_size || !pinfo->dsc.initial_dec_delay ||
+	    !pinfo->dsc.scale_increment_interval ||
+	    !pinfo->dsc.nfl_bpg_offset || !pinfo->dsc.slice_bpg_offset ||
+	    !pinfo->dsc.final_offset) {
+		dev_err(pinfo->panel.dev,
+			"TB371FC DSC parameters were not populated before prepare\n");
+		return -EINVAL;
+	}
+
 	mipi_dsi_dual_dcs_write_seq_multi(&dsi_ctx, dsi0, dsi1, 0xff, 0x20);
 	mipi_dsi_dual_dcs_write_seq_multi(&dsi_ctx, dsi0, dsi1, 0xfb, 0x01);
 	mipi_dsi_dual_dcs_write_seq_multi(&dsi_ctx, dsi0, dsi1, 0x32, 0x72);
